  "description": "A parametric STOVE on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE BURNERS ARE A CIRCLE ROW, not rings. render-2d's circle kind reads a centre list whose THIRD COLUMN is the per-circle radius — so all four (or two, or five) burners are one row, one colour, one layer, and the count changes by swapping which centre list is selected. A ring per burner would be four times the geometry to say the same thing.\n\nTYPE DECIDES WHERE THE BODY STARTS. A Built-in hob is the same object with its carcass collapsed to the hob slab — base height becomes rim height minus hob thickness and the oven door disappears — so a hob dropped into a counter and a freestanding cooker are one flow.\n\nOVEN VOLUME is published at 60% of the carcass box, because a cavity is not its enclosure, and it reads 0 for a hob, which is the honest answer rather than a small number.",
